[{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q1","number":1,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions in this section require the use of Partial Fractions, Improper Integrals, Integration of Inverse Trigonometric Functions and Integration of Hyperbolic Functions.</strong></p><p>Find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{1-x^2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\,dx=\\arcsin x+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\,dx=\\arctan x+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\,dx=\\operatorname{arcosh}x+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}\\,dx=\\arsinh x+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{1}{1-x^2}\\,dx=\\artanh x+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q2","number":2,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}6\\cot x\\,dx=\\ln k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive integer.</p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/2}6\\cot x\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is undefined.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}6\\cot x\\,dx\n =6\\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\\,dx\n=6\\left[\\ln|\\sin x|\\right]_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6\\left(\\ln 1-\\ln\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\right)\n=-6\\ln\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}=\\ln 8.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The integral is improper because <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cot 0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is undefined.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^{\\pi/2}6\\cot x\\,dx\n=\\lim_{a\\to0^+}\\int_a^{\\pi/2}6\\cot x\\,dx\n=\\lim_{a\\to0^+}\\left(6\\ln\\left|\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right|-6\\ln|\\sin a|\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin a\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln|\\sin a|\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The integral diverges and is undefined.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q3","number":3,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the substitution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> transforms <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{25\\cos^2x+\\sin^2x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{25+u^2}\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\arctan 5}\\frac{1}{25\\cos^2x+\\sin^2x}\\,dx=k\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a rational number to be found.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"du=\\sec^2x\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\cos^2x\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{1}{25\\cos^2x+\\sin^2x}\\,dx\n =\\int\\frac{\\cos^2x}{25\\cos^2x+\\sin^2x}\\,du\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\int\\frac{1}{25+\\tan^2x}\\,du\n=\\int\\frac{1}{25+u^2}\\,du.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>With <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the limits <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\arctan5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> become <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^{\\arctan5}\\frac{1}{25\\cos^2x+\\sin^2x}\\,dx\n =\\int_0^5\\frac{1}{25+u^2}\\,du\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac1{25}\\int_0^5\\frac{1}{1+(u/5)^2}\\,du\n=\\frac15\\left[\\arctan\\left(\\frac u5\\right)\\right]_0^5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac15\\left(\\frac\\pi4-0\\right)=\\frac\\pi{20}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac1{20}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_{\\sqrt{\\ln 2}}^{\\sqrt{\\ln 5}}\\frac{x}{\\sinh(x^2)}\\,dx=\\frac12\\ln 2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"du=2x\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The limits become <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\ln2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\ln5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI =\\int_{\\sqrt{\\ln2}}^{\\sqrt{\\ln5}}\\frac{x}{\\sinh(x^2)}\\,dx\n=\\frac12\\int_{\\ln2}^{\\ln5}\\frac{1}{\\sinh u}\\,du\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac12\\int_{\\ln2}^{\\ln5}\\frac{2e^u}{e^{2u}-1}\\,du.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Set <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=e^u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"du=dv/v\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; the limits become <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI =\\int_2^5\\frac{1}{v^2-1}\\,dv\n=\\frac12\\int_2^5\\left(\\frac1{v-1}-\\frac1{v+1}\\right)\\,dv\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac12\\left[\\ln|v-1|-\\ln|v+1|\\right]_2^5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac12\\left((\\ln4-\\ln6)-(\\ln1-\\ln3)\\right)\n=\\frac12\\ln2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q5","number":5,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{x^2-12x+61}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_5^7\\left(3-\\frac{78}{x^2-12x+61}\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle y=3-\\frac{78}{x^2-12x+61}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> intersects the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>The curve has a stationary point at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the exact area of the region between the curve, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Complete the square:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx^2-12x+61=(x-6)^2+25.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{1}{x^2-12x+61}\\,dx\n=\\frac1{25}\\int\\frac{1}{1+((x-6)/5)^2}\\,dx\n=\\frac15\\arctan\\left(\\frac{x-6}{5}\\right)+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_5^7\\left(3-\\frac{78}{x^2-12x+61}\\right)\\,dx\n =\\left[3x-\\frac{78}{5}\\arctan\\left(\\frac{x-6}{5}\\right)\\right]_5^7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6-\\frac{156}{5}\\arctan\\left(\\frac15\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c i)</h3><p>At an <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-intercept, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n0 =3-\\frac{78}{x^2-12x+61},\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n0 =x^2-12x+35=(x-5)(x-7).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(5,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q=(7,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c ii)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{156(x-6)}{(x^2-12x+61)^2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At a stationary point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny\\big|_{x=6}=3-\\frac{78}{36-72+61}=3-\\frac{78}{25}=-\\frac3{25}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=(6,-3/25)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c iii)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_5^6\\left(3-\\frac{78}{x^2-12x+61}\\right)\\,dx\n =\\left[3x-\\frac{78}{5}\\arctan\\left(\\frac{x-6}{5}\\right)\\right]_5^6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =3-\\frac{78}{5}\\arctan\\left(\\frac15\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The curve lies below the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis on this interval, so the exact area is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{78}{5}\\arctan\\left(\\frac15\\right)-3\\quad\\text{units}^2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q6","number":6,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{2x^3+x^2+x}{(x+1)(x^2+1)}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\frac{2x^3+x^2+x}{(x+1)(x^2+1)}\\,dx=2-\\ln2-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Write</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{2x^3+x^2+x}{(x+1)(x^2+1)}=A+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{Cx+D}{x^2+1}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Equating coefficients gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{2x^3+x^2+x}{(x+1)(x^2+1)}\\,dx\n =\\int\\left(2-\\frac1{x+1}-\\frac1{x^2+1}\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2x-\\ln|x+1|-\\arctan x+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^1\\frac{2x^3+x^2+x}{(x+1)(x^2+1)}\\,dx\n =\\left[2x-\\ln|x+1|-\\arctan x\\right]_0^1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2-\\ln2-\\frac\\pi4.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>By using a suitable substitution, show that:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_{-5/2}^{-3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x^2+20x+34}}\\,dx=\\frac12\\ln\\left(\\frac{2+\\sqrt{13}}{3}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_{1/2}^{5/4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-4x^2+4x+8}}\\,dx=\\frac{\\pi}{12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_{(\\sqrt3-3)/2}^{0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x^2+12x+18}}\\,dx=\\frac{\\pi}{72}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_3^4\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-4x^2+28x-40}}\\,dx=\\frac16\\ln2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Complete the square: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x^2+20x+34=9+4(x+5/2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sinh u=2(x+5/2)/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\tfrac32\\cosh u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-5/2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3/2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\arsinh(2/3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI=\\frac12\\int_0^{\\arsinh(2/3)}du\n=\\frac12\\arsinh\\frac23\n=\\frac12\\ln\\left(\\frac{2+\\sqrt{13}}{3}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Complete the square: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4x^2+4x+8=9-4(x-1/2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin u=2(x-1/2)/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\tfrac32\\cos u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The limits become <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi/6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI=\\frac12\\int_0^{\\pi/6}du=\\frac\\pi{12}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Complete the square: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x^2+12x+18=9+4(x+3/2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan u=2(x+3/2)/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\tfrac32\\sec^2u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The limits become <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi/6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi/4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI=\\frac16\\int_{\\pi/6}^{\\pi/4}du=\\frac16\\left(\\frac\\pi4-\\frac\\pi6\\right)=\\frac\\pi{72}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Complete the square: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4x^2+28x-40=9-4(x-7/2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tanh u=2(x-7/2)/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\tfrac32\\sech^2u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The limits <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3,4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> give <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=-\\artanh(1/3),\\artanh(1/3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, respectively. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI =\\frac16\\int_{-\\artanh(1/3)}^{\\artanh(1/3)}du\n=\\frac13\\artanh\\frac13\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac16\\ln\\left(\\frac{1+1/3}{1-1/3}\\right)=\\frac16\\ln2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.32-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_{-1/\\sqrt3}^{1/\\sqrt3}\\frac{12x^2}{1-x^4}\\,dx=3\\ln(p+\\sqrt q)+r\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p>","steps":["<p>Factor the denominator and use partial fractions:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n1-x^4=(1-x)(1+x)(1+x^2),\\qquad\n\\frac{12x^2}{1-x^4}=\\frac3{1-x}+\\frac3{1+x}-\\frac6{1+x^2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI =\\left[-3\\ln|1-x|+3\\ln|1+x|-6\\arctan x\\right]_{-1/\\sqrt3}^{1/\\sqrt3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =3\\ln(2+\\sqrt3)-\\pi-\\left(3\\ln(2-\\sqrt3)+\\pi\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =3\\ln(7+4\\sqrt3)-2\\pi.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=48\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]}]